Dtrace script has the following parts:

<a> PROBE:
    Probes are addressed using the P:M:F:N (Provider Module Function Name) format. Skipping any 
    of the fields of the tuple act as the "*" wildcard.  A probe can also have arguments that are referenced
    using arg0....arg9 or arg[n].

<b> PREDICATE:
    Once the probe is hit the predicate is tested to check if the clause should be executed. Think of it as 
    the condition in a conditional breakpoint.

<c> CLAUSE:
    The main program body that gets executed when the probe/predicate allow it to do so.


Variables:
	-> Global scope (by default and declared anywhere)
	-> Thread scope (self->varname)
	-> Clause scope (this->varname)


